 "criterion": "`release plan --from-release-commit` fails with E165 and writes no output file in any of these cases: HEAD is not the given commit; the commit neither adds nor modifies the decision file; it deletes no direct-child changeset `.md` file (nested Markdown files and `README.md` do not count); a claimed package's manifest does not change to its claimed version; a claimed package's changelog is unchanged; an unclaimed manifest version changes; a claimed package is not found; or the commit changes any path other than a manifest (`Cargo.toml`, `package.json`, `pyproject.toml`) or lockfile (`Cargo.lock`, `package-lock.json`, `npm-shrinkwrap.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `yarn.lock`, `bun.lock`, `bun.lockb`, `uv.lock`, `poetry.lock`, `pdm.lock`) anywhere, a package's changelog, the decision file, a direct-child changeset, or the changesets directory's `pre.json`.",
 "is_error_case": true
}
{
 "id": "REL-AUTH-03",
 "criterion": "A committed decision file whose digest does not match its entries fails with E166. Each target version is parsed using the grammar of its package ecosystem; durable operation IDs, artifact slots and registry observations bound to an operation use that same grammar. Version values remain strings on the wire, and decision schema versions 1 and 2 are accepted; any other version fails with an error naming the version found.",
 "is_error_case": true
}
{
 "id": "REL-AUTH-04",
 "criterion": "An abbreviated or unknown `--from-release-commit` SHA, a non-40-hex `--orchestration-revision` for a source with `[release]`, or an `--intent` file with a different `schemaVersion` (`E215`, naming found and expected versions) fails before any output file is written or any effect runs.",
 "is_error_case": true
}
{
 "id": "REL-AUTH-05",
 "criterion": "`release plan` and `release execute` require the source checkout at a detached HEAD and fail with E170 otherwise. `callisto release` accepts an attached HEAD. Every route requires a complete, non-shallow SHA-1 repository and fails with E266 otherwise.",
 "is_error_case": true
}
{
 "id": "REL-AUTH-06",
 "criterion": "`release execute` re-derives the plan from the source checkout and fails with E124 before any effect when the result differs from the `--intent` file. A change to the decision, source commit, manifests, config, registry binding or origin remote is enough.",
 "is_error_case": true
}
{
 "id": "REL-AUTH-07",
 "criterion": "Before each operation, the executor re-checks HEAD, worktree cleanliness and the `origin` push URL. A change stops the run before that operation's effect, with E124 for a moved HEAD or remote and E267 for a dirty worktree.",
 "is_error_case": true
}
{
 "id": "REL-AUTH-08",
 "criterion": "`release plan` for a source with `[release]` requires `--orchestration-revision` and `--artifact-repository` (`E231`). For a source without `[release]` it ignores both flags, prints a notice, and plans zero artifact slots.",
 "is_error_case": true
}
{
 "id": "REL-AUTH-09",
 "criterion": "`[release].forge-repository` is the only GitHub destination. Planning rejects an `--artifact-repository` that differs from it (`E230`) or from the `origin` GitHub repository (E175). Execution rejects artifact slots that target another repository, and a `[release]` section without it fails planning with E198.",
 "is_error_case": true
}
{
 "id": "REL-ORD-01",
 "criterion": "A graph package has one tag, GitHub release draft and publish, however many ecosystems it publishes to. Its tag is created only after all selected registry publishes belonging to its canonical manifests succeed, in every ecosystem a dual Cargo and npm package publishes to, and its GitHub release draft only after its tag. A `[[release.artifact]]` slot's upload follows the product's draft and gates the product's publish even when a different selected package owns the asset, and the product's publish also waits for the tag of that package, which follows its registry publishes, so the release is published only after the draft, every upload and every publish behind them."
}
{
 "id": "REL-ORD-02",
 "criterion": "A selected package publishes after the selected packages it depends on through runtime, build, optional or dev edges, and waits for the dependency's distribution in the ecosystem of the declaring manifest, so a Cargo dependent follows a dual package's crate and an npm dependent follows its npm package. An npm dependent follows the dependency's publish command, not the registry showing the version. A dev edge between two packages in the same dependency cycle does not order them, and a runtime, build or optional cycle fails with E104."
}
{
 "id": "REL-ORD-03",
 "criterion": "An npm package with attached platform packages publishes each platform package with `npm publish <platform-dir>` before publishing the owner package. Operations start one at a time and a failed publish command stops the run, so an owner package is never published after the command for one of its platform packages fails."
}
{
 "id": "REL-ORD-04",
 "criterion": "An npm registry publish, platform packages included, is issued without waiting for the registry to show the version, and stays unconfirmed. Another npm publish may then start, but no tag, GitHub release draft, upload or publication does until the registry has shown the version of every publish behind it. When no operation can start, Callisto looks at every unconfirmed publish together and waits between looks, 15 s, 45 s, 2 minutes, then 3 minute steps, for as long as the longest `confirm-timeout` among them (default 6 minutes), so the wait is the slowest registry's and not the sum. That window opens when the first of the publishes is issued and runs on the clock, so the time spent looking counts, and a publish that is shown along the way does not start it again or restart the 15 s, 45 s, 2 minute schedule. A look's own retries, including a registry's `Retry-After`, wait no longer in total than the window has left, and a look made with none left tries once. A publish still not shown then fails the run with E157, naming the first, and no receipt is written; a rerun adopts every version already published. Cargo and PyPI publishes are confirmed as they are published.",
 "is_error_case": true
}

